# Solid SSR hydration

Solid hydration needs one `sharedConfig` singleton. If SSR `renderToStringAsync` and the compiled component load two copies of `solid-js`, HTML has no `data-hk` and the client errors (`Client-only API called on the server side`).

- Never put `solid-js` or `solid-js/web` in `ssr.noExternal`.
- Keep `avalon:solid-oxc-exclude` `resolveId`: SSR → `dist/server.js`, client → `dist/dev.js`.
- `vite-plugin-solid` must use `hot: false` (solid-refresh shifts hydration keys).
- After resolution/SSR config changes, clear `www/node_modules/.vite`.
- `data-hk` is Solid’s; `data-solid-render-id` is Avalon’s on `<avalon-island>`.
